From: Sisyphus <local@example.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: airoha: add restart handler

The Airoha EN7581/AN7583 SoCs use the stock carrier U-Boot/ATF which
performs a warm (DDR-unretraining) reset when PSCI SYSTEM_RESET is
invoked, causing boot failures (UBI attach corruption, kernel panic)
after soft reboot on devices like the Nokia XG-040G-MF.

The watchdog, on the other hand, drives the SoC through the full
hardware reset path (the same one used at power-on), which correctly
re-initializes the DDR controller.

Register a restart handler that arms the watchdog with the shortest
possible timeout, triggering an immediate hardware reset.

The restart handler must preempt PSCI (priority 129): PSCI SYSTEM_RESET
takes the bootloader's warm-reset path which does not re-train DDR,
while the watchdog drives the full hardware reset path. The watchdog
core defaults to priority 0 (last resort), which would never fire
before PSCI.

Signed-off-by: Sisyphus <local@example.com>
---
 drivers/watchdog/airoha_wdt.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/airoha_wdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/airoha_wdt.c
--- a/drivers/watchdog/airoha_wdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/airoha_wdt.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/math.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/watchdog.h>
@@ -89,6 +90,31 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static int airoha_wdt_restart(struct watchdog_device *wdog_dev,
+			      unsigned long action, void *data)
+{
+	struct airoha_wdt_desc *airoha_wdt = watchdog_get_drvdata(wdog_dev);
+	u32 val;
+
+	/* Arm the watchdog with the shortest possible timeout to
+	 * trigger an immediate SoC hardware reset.
+	 *
+	 * A plain watchdog timeout reset is used instead of PSCI
+	 * SYSTEM_RESET because the stock bootloader's warm reset path
+	 * does not re-train the DDR controller, which makes the system
+	 * fail to attach the UBI rootfs after a soft reboot.
+	 */
+	writel(0x1, airoha_wdt->base + WDT_TIMER_LOAD_VALUE);
+	val = readl(airoha_wdt->base + TIMER_CTRL);
+	val |= (WDT_TIMER_ENABLE | WDT_ENABLE | WDT_TIMER_INTERRUPT);
+	writel(val, airoha_wdt->base + TIMER_CTRL);
+
+	/* Wait for the reset to happen, or time out and report failure. */
+	mdelay(100);
+
+	return -ETIMEDOUT;
+}
+
 static int airoha_wdt_set_timeout(struct watchdog_device *wdog_dev, unsigned int timeout)
 {
 	wdog_dev->timeout = timeout;
@@ -122,6 +148,7 @@
 	.ping = airoha_wdt_ping,
 	.set_timeout = airoha_wdt_set_timeout,
 	.get_timeleft = airoha_wdt_get_timeleft,
+	.restart = airoha_wdt_restart,
 };
 
 static int airoha_wdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
@@ -161,6 +188,13 @@
 	watchdog_set_nowayout(wdog_dev, nowayout);
 	watchdog_stop_on_unregister(wdog_dev);
 
+	/* Preempt PSCI (priority 129) on restart: the stock bootloader's
+	 * PSCI SYSTEM_RESET warm-reset path does not re-train DDR, which
+	 * makes the system crash after soft reboot. The watchdog drives
+	 * the SoC through the full hardware reset path instead.
+	 */
+	watchdog_set_restart_priority(wdog_dev, 255);
+
 	ret = devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, wdog_dev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
